<title>FRANCE: New York top ex-Paris cargo destination in Dec '96.</title>
<headline>New York top ex-Paris cargo destination in Dec '96.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports last month.</p>
<p>The top ten ex-Paris air cargo destinations in December 1996 in tonnes and the percentage change on December 1995, were</p>
<p>			     Dec 96	percent change:</p>
<p>  1.  New York	    3,314	down    2.0</p>
<p>  2.  Chicago	     2,158	  up   20.1</p>
<p>  3.  Hong Kong	   1,966	down    8.2</p>
<p>  4.  Tokyo		 1,940	down   13.7</p>
<p>  5.  Mexico City	 1,250	  up   58.5</p>
<p>  6.  Singapore	   1,090	  up   70.6</p>
<p>  7.  Montreal	    1,049	down   10.5</p>
<p>  8.  Sao Paulo	   1,043	down    7.9</p>
<p>  9.  Los Angeles	 1,038	  up    8.8</p>
<p> 10.  Seoul		   793	  up   22.4</p>
<p>-- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
